### === Day 9 Exercise 2: Register and Login ===

### Register success
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Siti Aminah",
  "email": "siti@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Login success
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "siti@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Duplicate email error (register with the same email again)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Siti Aminah",
  "email": "siti@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Wrong password error
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "siti@example.com",
  "password": "wrongPassword"
}

### === Day 9 Exercise 3: Protect Ticket Endpoints ===

### Step 1: Login as the seeded admin (role=ADMIN) to get an admin token
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "admin12345"
}

### Step 2: Login as the user registered in Exercise 2 (role=USER) to get a user token
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "siti@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Test 1: GET /api/tickets without token -> expect 401
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets

### Test 2: GET /api/tickets with USER token -> expect 200
# Replace TOKEN with the token from Step 2
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### Test 3: POST /api/tickets with USER token -> expect 403
# Replace TOKEN with the token from Step 2
POST http://localhost:8081/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Printer not working",
  "description": "Office printer on 3rd floor is jammed.",
  "category": "Hardware",
  "priority": "LOW",
  "createdBy": "siti@example.com"
}

### Test 4: POST /api/tickets with ADMIN token -> expect 201
# Replace TOKEN with the token from Step 1
POST http://localhost:8081/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Printer not working",
  "description": "Office printer on 3rd floor is jammed.",
  "category": "Hardware",
  "priority": "LOW",
  "createdBy": "siti@example.com"
}

### Health check
GET http://localhost:8081/api/health

### About info
GET http://localhost:8081/api/about

### List tickets
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets

### Filter tickets by status
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets?status=OPEN

### Filter tickets by priority
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets?priority=HIGH

### Filter tickets by category
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets?category=Email

### Get paged tickets (defaults: page=0, size=5, sortBy=createdAt, direction=desc)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets/paged

### Get paged tickets - page 0, size 5
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5

### Get paged tickets - page 1, size 5
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets/paged?page=1&size=5

### Get paged tickets sorted by createdAt descending (explicit)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=createdAt&direction=desc

### Get paged tickets sorted by priority ascending
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=priority&direction=asc

### Get existing ticket
# Replace the ID below with an actual ID returned by GET /api/tickets
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ID

### Get missing ticket
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets/000000000000000000000000

### Create ticket (valid)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "VPN connection not working",
  "description": "User cannot connect to company VPN from home.",
  "category": "Network",
  "priority": "MEDIUM",
  "createdBy": "siti@example.com"
}

### Create ticket (invalid)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "",
  "category": "",
  "priority": "",
  "createdBy": ""
}

### === Day 8 Exercise 5: Query Behaviour and Troubleshooting ===

### Test 1: Invalid status value
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets?status=INVALID

### Test 2: Invalid priority value
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets?priority=URGENT

### Test 3: Page number with no records
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets/paged?page=99&size=5

### Test 4: Very large page size
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=100

### Test 5: Unknown sort field
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=unknownField&direction=asc

### Test 6: Combined filters (status + priority)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/tickets?status=OPEN&priority=HIGH
